02:12:15,040 --> 02:12:17,040
the philosophy he or she is trying

3445
02:12:17,040 --> 02:12:19,040
to get across.

3446
02:12:19,040 --> 02:12:21,040
Anne Rand was probably better at that than anybody else

3447
02:12:21,040 --> 02:12:23,040
I could possibly think of.

3448
02:12:23,040 --> 02:12:25,040
Atlas Shrugged, some of those towering novels.

3449
02:12:25,040 --> 02:12:27,040
The novel kept us intrigued,

3450
02:12:27,040 --> 02:12:29,040
but guess what she was doing all the time?

3451
02:12:29,040 --> 02:12:31,040
Feeding us her philosophy. Feeding us her

3452
02:12:31,040 --> 02:12:33,040
philosophy. Now whether you agreed with her

3453
02:12:33,040 --> 02:12:35,040
philosophy or not, you had to admit she was really

3454
02:12:35,040 --> 02:12:37,040
good at getting it out there.

3455
02:12:37,040 --> 02:12:39,040
Weaving it through the story.

3456
02:12:39,040 --> 02:12:41,040
In the dialogue and in the speeches

3457
02:12:41,040 --> 02:12:43,040
and in the text. Fabulous.

3458
02:12:43,040 --> 02:12:45,040
Novels. Novels are good.

3459
02:12:47,040 --> 02:12:49,040
Now here's a little personal advice. Skip the trash.

3460
02:12:49,040 --> 02:12:51,040
I mean, you don't...

3461
02:12:51,040 --> 02:12:55,040
Sometimes you can find something valuable in a trashy novel.

3462
02:12:55,040 --> 02:12:57,040
I wouldn't go through it to find it.

3463
02:12:59,040 --> 02:13:00,040
You can find a crust

3464
02:13:00,040 --> 02:13:01,040
of bread in a garbage can,

3465
02:13:01,040 --> 02:13:03,040
but I wouldn't go through it.

3466
02:13:03,040 --> 02:13:05,040
Number one, you don't need

3467
02:13:05,040 --> 02:13:07,040
the reputation.

3468
02:13:07,040 --> 02:13:09,040
So,

3469
02:13:09,040 --> 02:13:11,040
not enough time to read the brilliant stuff,

3470
02:13:11,040 --> 02:13:13,040
the good stuff.

3471
02:13:13,040 --> 02:13:15,040
Skip the trash, really.

3472
02:13:15,040 --> 02:13:17,040
My personal advice on personal development.

3473
02:13:17,040 --> 02:13:19,040
Becoming more valuable than you are.

3474
02:13:19,040 --> 02:13:21,040
Key.

3475
02:13:21,040 --> 02:13:23,040
Next is biographies

3476
02:13:23,040 --> 02:13:25,040
and autobiographies. The story of

3477
02:13:25,040 --> 02:13:27,040
stories of successful people,

3478
02:13:27,040 --> 02:13:29,040
unsuccessful people.

3479
02:13:31,040 --> 02:13:33,040
There's some dramatic stuff.

3480
02:13:33,040 --> 02:13:35,040
Right?

3481
02:13:35,040 --> 02:13:37,040
Over the last hundred years it's been written.

3482
02:13:37,040 --> 02:13:39,040
Biographies and autobiographies.

3483
02:13:39,040 --> 02:13:41,040
Here's one of the best. The Bible.

3484
02:13:41,040 --> 02:13:43,040
The Bible is a unique book

3485
02:13:43,040 --> 02:13:45,040
because it's got a list of human stories

3486
02:13:45,040 --> 02:13:46,040
on one side of the

3487
02:13:46,040 --> 02:13:47,040
ledger, another list of human stories

3488
02:13:47,040 --> 02:13:49,040
on the other side of the ledger.

3489
02:13:49,040 --> 02:13:51,040
One's called examples and the other's called warnings.

3490
02:13:51,040 --> 02:13:53,040
And here's what we've got to have

3491
02:13:53,040 --> 02:13:55,040
on biographies and autobiographies.

3492
02:13:55,040 --> 02:13:57,040
Both warnings and examples.

3493
02:13:59,040 --> 02:14:01,040
In the Bible, the examples.

3494
02:14:01,040 --> 02:14:03,040
The Bible says, look at these people's lives.

3495
02:14:03,040 --> 02:14:05,040
Follow them. Follow their philosophy.

3496
02:14:05,040 --> 02:14:07,040
Follow their advice.

3497
02:14:07,040 --> 02:14:09,040
Then we've got the warnings. Right?

3498
02:14:09,040 --> 02:14:11,040
Biographies people did. They messed up their life

3499
02:14:11,040 --> 02:14:13,040
and threw their life away.

3500
02:14:13,040 --> 02:14:15,040
Vaguely important. Both sides of the scenario.

3501
02:14:17,040 --> 02:14:18,040
Now if your life story ever

3502
02:14:18,040 --> 02:14:19,040
gets in one of those books,

3503
02:14:19,040 --> 02:14:20,040
make sure they use it

3504
02:14:20,040 --> 02:14:21,040
as an example, not a warning.

3505
02:14:29,040 --> 02:14:31,040
Also we need balance.

3506
02:14:31,040 --> 02:14:33,040
Both sides. Balance. Good and evil.

3507
02:14:33,040 --> 02:14:35,040
Biographies, autobiographies.

3508
02:14:39,040 --> 02:14:41,040
You need a book on Gandhi?

3509
02:14:41,040 --> 02:14:43,040
You need a book on Hitler?

3510
02:14:45,040 --> 02:14:47,040
One to illustrate

3511
02:14:47,040 --> 02:14:49,040
how high a human being can go

3512
02:14:49,040 --> 02:14:51,040
and the other one to illustrate

3513
02:14:51,040 --> 02:14:53,040
what?

3514
02:14:53,040 --> 02:14:55,040
How low and despicable

3515
02:14:55,040 --> 02:14:57,040
a human being can become.

3516
02:14:57,040 --> 02:14:59,040
We need both sides of the scenario.

3517
02:15:03,040 --> 02:15:05,040
Next. Accounting.

3518
02:15:05,040 --> 02:15:07,040
Got to have a little, at least primary

3519
02:15:07,040 --> 02:15:09,040
view of accounting.

3520
02:15:09,040 --> 02:15:11,040
Kids have got to start learning

3521
02:15:11,040 --> 02:15:13,040
the difference between a debit and a credit.

3522
02:15:19,040 --> 02:15:21,040
Next is law. We all need, right,

3523
02:15:21,040 --> 02:15:23,040
a little bit. You don't have to be a lawyer

3524
02:15:23,040 --> 02:15:25,040
but you got to know contracts.

3525
02:15:25,040 --> 02:15:27,040
What to sign, what not to sign.

3526
02:15:27,040 --> 02:15:29,040
Backups. Good advice.

3527
02:15:29,040 --> 02:15:31,040
How to be safe rather than sorry.

3528
02:15:31,040 --> 02:15:33,040
All of us need

3529
02:15:33,040 --> 02:15:35,040
a little law. Not a lawyer

3530
02:15:35,040 --> 02:15:37,040
but a little law.

3531
02:15:37,040 --> 02:15:39,040
Especially these complicated ones.

3532
02:15:39,040 --> 02:15:41,040
These complicated days.

3533
02:15:41,040 --> 02:15:43,040
Everything's in court these days.

3534
02:15:45,040 --> 02:15:47,040
I learned this the hard way.

3535
02:15:49,040 --> 02:15:51,040
Company wanted to borrow money.

3536
02:15:51,040 --> 02:15:53,040
Long time ago.

3537
02:15:53,040 --> 02:15:55,040
Up in Canada.

3538
02:15:55,040 --> 02:15:57,040
Company wanted to borrow some money.

3539
02:15:57,040 --> 02:15:59,040
The bank said, well, yes,

3540
02:15:59,040 --> 02:16:01,040
we will loan the company the money

3541
02:16:01,040 --> 02:16:03,040
if Mr. Rohn will sign

3542
02:16:03,040 --> 02:16:05,040
personally.

3543
02:16:05,040 --> 02:16:07,040
And I wanted

3544
02:16:07,040 --> 02:16:08,040
to play hero and I

3545
02:16:08,040 --> 02:16:09,040
knew the company could pay it.

3546
02:16:09,040 --> 02:16:11,040
Quarter of a million dollars.

3547
02:16:11,040 --> 02:16:13,040
So I signed.

3548
02:16:13,040 --> 02:16:15,040
No problem.

3549
02:16:15,040 --> 02:16:16,040
Sure enough, within less than a

3550
02:16:16,040 --> 02:16:17,040
year they paid it all back.

3551
02:16:17,040 --> 02:16:19,040
Quarter of a million dollars.

3552
02:16:19,040 --> 02:16:21,040
I am now a hero.

3553
02:16:21,040 --> 02:16:23,040
Well,

3554
02:16:23,040 --> 02:16:25,040
about a year later

3555
02:16:25,040 --> 02:16:27,040
this company gets in financial trouble.

3556
02:16:27,040 --> 02:16:29,040
They go back to the bank

3557
02:16:29,040 --> 02:16:31,040
and borrow this quarter of a million dollars

3558
02:16:31,040 --> 02:16:33,040
again.

3559
02:16:33,040 --> 02:16:35,040
I said,

3560
02:16:35,040 --> 02:16:37,040
I hope my phone doesn't ring because

3561
02:16:37,040 --> 02:16:39,040
I won't sign the note this time.

3562
02:16:39,040 --> 02:16:41,040
I knew they were in trouble.

3563
02:16:41,040 --> 02:16:43,040
I knew they were probably going to go bankrupt.

3564
02:16:43,040 --> 02:16:45,040
My phone never rang.

3565
02:16:47,040 --> 02:16:49,040
I'm off the hook.

3566
02:16:49,040 --> 02:16:51,040
Sure enough, within less than a year

3567
02:16:51,040 --> 02:16:53,040
the company goes bankrupt. Can't pay.

3568
02:16:53,040 --> 02:16:55,040
But I get this letter from the bank saying,

3569
02:16:55,040 --> 02:16:57,040
Dear Mr. Rohn,

3570
02:16:57,040 --> 02:16:59,040
Since the company cannot perform its obligation

3571
02:16:59,040 --> 02:17:01,040
and pay this quarter of a million dollars,

3572
02:17:01,040 --> 02:17:03,040
and since we have here your personal guarantee,

3573
02:17:03,040 --> 02:17:05,040
would you please send us your check

3574
02:17:05,040 --> 02:17:07,040
for a quarter of a million dollars?

3575
02:17:07,040 --> 02:17:09,040
I said, hey, hold it, hold it.

3576
02:17:09,040 --> 02:17:11,040
There must be some mistake here.

3577
02:17:11,040 --> 02:17:13,040
I signed that first note

3578
02:17:13,040 --> 02:17:15,040
and they paid it all back.

3579
02:17:15,040 --> 02:17:17,040
I wouldn't have signed the second note.

3580
02:17:17,040 --> 02:17:19,040
I didn't sign the second note.

3581
02:17:19,040 --> 02:17:21,040
Well,

3582
02:17:21,040 --> 02:17:23,040
what I didn't know I had originally signed

3583
02:17:23,040 --> 02:17:25,040
was a continuing guarantee.

3584
02:17:27,040 --> 02:17:29,040
So, now I know

3585
02:17:29,040 --> 02:17:31,040
what the word continuing means.

3586
02:17:39,040 --> 02:17:43,040
I'm asking you to study a little law,

3587
02:17:43,040 --> 02:17:45,040
know what to sign,

3588
02:17:45,040 --> 02:17:47,040
know how to defend yourself,

3589
02:17:47,040 --> 02:17:49,040
say, hey, we'll get back,

3590
02:17:49,040 --> 02:17:51,040
don't sign too quickly.

3591
02:17:51,040 --> 02:17:53,040
I mean, there's all kinds of things here.

3592
02:17:53,040 --> 02:17:55,040
Be a student.

3593
02:17:55,040 --> 02:17:57,040
Don't be lazy in learning.

3594
02:17:57,040 --> 02:17:59,040
How to defend as well as nourish.

3595
02:17:59,040 --> 02:18:00,040
How to grow as well

3596
02:18:00,040 --> 02:18:01,040
as take care of your enemies.

3597
02:18:01,040 --> 02:18:03,040
You've got to learn.

3598
02:18:03,040 --> 02:18:05,040
Let your library indicate that you're a serious student

3599
02:18:05,040 --> 02:18:07,040
about personal relationships with your family,

3600
02:18:07,040 --> 02:18:09,040
gifts and skills,

3601
02:18:09,040 --> 02:18:11,040
economics,

3602
02:18:11,040 --> 02:18:13,040
and all the rest.

3603
02:18:13,040 --> 02:18:15,040
Here's the next one.

3604
02:18:15,040 --> 02:18:17,040
Economics.

3605
02:18:17,040 --> 02:18:18,040
We're going to study that when

3606
02:18:18,040 --> 02:18:19,040
we come back from our break.

3607
02:18:21,040 --> 02:18:23,040
Economics. We're going to cover,

3608
02:18:23,040 --> 02:18:24,040
especially for the kids today,

3609
02:18:24,040 --> 02:18:25,040
how to become financially independent.

3610
02:18:25,040 --> 02:18:27,040
We're going to let the adults listen.

3611
02:18:29,040 --> 02:18:31,040
I've been teaching kids for the last 18, 19 years

3612
02:18:31,040 --> 02:18:33,040
how to be rich by 40,

3613
02:18:33,040 --> 02:18:35,040
35 if you're extra bright.

3614
02:18:35,040 --> 02:18:37,040
Most kids think they're extra bright, they go for 35.

3615
02:18:37,040 --> 02:18:39,040
Or much sooner

3616
02:18:39,040 --> 02:18:41,040
they find a unique opportunity.

3617
02:18:41,040 --> 02:18:43,040
We're going to get into that.

3618
02:18:43,040 --> 02:18:45,040
Be a student of economics.

3619
02:18:45,040 --> 02:18:47,040
Next, culture, sophistication.

3620
02:18:47,040 --> 02:18:49,040
Don't leave that out of your life.

3621
02:18:49,040 --> 02:18:51,040
Culture, sophistication.

3622
02:18:51,040 --> 02:18:53,040
Culture is part of the fabric of the nation.

3623
02:18:53,040 --> 02:18:55,040
Culture is what makes us different

3624
02:18:55,040 --> 02:18:57,040
than dogs and animals.

3625
02:18:57,040 --> 02:18:59,040
Culture is what makes us

3626
02:18:59,040 --> 02:19:01,040
different from the barbarians.

3627
02:19:01,040 --> 02:19:03,040
Culture,

3628
02:19:03,040 --> 02:19:05,040
sophistication.

3629
02:19:05,040 --> 02:19:07,040
Be a student of the dance

3630
02:19:07,040 --> 02:19:08,040
and the art and the music,

3631
02:19:08,040 --> 02:19:09,040
and all the rest of it.

3632
02:19:09,040 --> 02:19:11,040
All the rest of those extraordinary

3633
02:19:11,040 --> 02:19:13,040
human values that are possible for us

3634
02:19:13,040 --> 02:19:15,040
all to participate in, as well as to enjoy.

3635
02:19:15,040 --> 02:19:17,040
Be a student of culture.

3636
02:19:19,040 --> 02:19:21,040
And the last one is spirituality.

3637
02:19:23,040 --> 02:19:25,040
Study it from the Bible

3638
02:19:25,040 --> 02:19:27,040
and all the related books about spirituality.

3639
02:19:27,040 --> 02:19:29,040
If you're a believer, study and practice.

3640
02:19:31,040 --> 02:19:33,040
Let your library show

3641
02:19:33,040 --> 02:19:35,040
you're a serious student.

3642
02:19:39,040 --> 02:19:41,040
Next, keep a journal.

3643
02:19:41,040 --> 02:19:43,040
Shelf said,

3644
02:19:43,040 --> 02:19:45,040
Mr. Owen, not only be a student,

3645
02:19:45,040 --> 02:19:47,040
but the good ideas

3646
02:19:47,040 --> 02:19:49,040
that you develop from the books.

3647
02:19:49,040 --> 02:19:51,040
Keep a separate journal.

3648
02:19:51,040 --> 02:19:53,040
Write all this stuff down.

3649
02:19:53,040 --> 02:19:55,040
Here's what he said.

3650
02:19:55,040 --> 02:19:57,040
Don't trust your memory.

3651
02:19:57,040 --> 02:19:59,040
If you're serious about becoming

3652
02:19:59,040 --> 02:20:01,040
wealthy and powerful and sophisticated

3653
02:20:01,040 --> 02:20:03,040
and healthy, influential,

3654
02:20:03,040 --> 02:20:05,040
cultured, unique,

3655
02:20:05,040 --> 02:20:07,040
keep a journal.

3656
02:20:07,040 --> 02:20:09,040
Don't trust your memory.

3657
02:20:09,040 --> 02:20:11,040
If you listen to something valuable,

3658
02:20:11,040 --> 02:20:13,040
write it down.

3659
02:20:13,040 --> 02:20:15,040
If you come across something important,

3660
02:20:15,040 --> 02:20:17,040
write it down.

3661
02:20:17,040 --> 02:20:19,040
Now, I used to take notes on pieces of paper

3662
02:20:19,040 --> 02:20:21,040
and torn off corners and backs of old envelopes

3663
02:20:21,040 --> 02:20:23,040
and restaurant placemats

3664
02:20:23,040 --> 02:20:25,040
and long sheets and narrow sheets

3665
02:20:25,040 --> 02:20:27,040
and little sheets and pieces

3666
02:20:27,040 --> 02:20:29,040
thrown in a drawer.

3667
02:20:29,040 --> 02:20:31,040
Found out, best way, keep a journal.

3668
02:20:31,040 --> 02:20:33,040
I've been keeping these journals now

3669
02:20:33,040 --> 02:20:35,040
since age 25.

3670
02:20:35,040 --> 02:20:37,040
It makes up a valuable part of my own learning

3671
02:20:37,040 --> 02:20:39,040
and it's a valuable part of my life.

3672
02:20:39,040 --> 02:20:41,040
I've been keeping them in my library.

3673
02:20:41,040 --> 02:20:43,040
My own journals now form a good portion

3674
02:20:43,040 --> 02:20:45,040
of my own library.

3675
02:20:45,040 --> 02:20:47,040
The stuff.

3676
02:20:47,040 --> 02:20:49,040
I'm trying to get kids to do like I do.

3677
02:20:49,040 --> 02:20:51,040
Be a buyer of empty books.

3678
02:20:51,040 --> 02:20:53,040
Kids find it interesting I buy an empty book.

3679
02:20:53,040 --> 02:20:55,040
Especially at my status in life.

3680
02:20:55,040 --> 02:20:57,040
What did I pay for this one?

3681
02:20:59,040 --> 02:21:01,040
Kids say, $26 for an empty book?

3682
02:21:03,040 --> 02:21:05,040
Why would you do that?

3683
02:21:05,040 --> 02:21:07,040
Well, the reason I paid $26 is

3684
02:21:07,040 --> 02:21:09,040
to press me.

3685
02:21:09,040 --> 02:21:11,040
To see if I can't find something worth $26

3686
02:21:11,040 --> 02:21:13,040
to put in here.

3687
02:21:13,040 --> 02:21:15,040
And I'm telling you, all my journals are private.

3688
02:21:15,040 --> 02:21:16,040
But if you got a

3689
02:21:16,040 --> 02:21:17,040
hold of one of my journals

3690
02:21:17,040 --> 02:21:19,040
you wouldn't have to look very far

3691
02:21:19,040 --> 02:21:21,040
until you would say,

3692
02:21:21,040 --> 02:21:23,040
this is worth more than $26.

3693
02:21:23,040 --> 02:21:25,040
I must admit,

3694
02:21:25,040 --> 02:21:27,040
if you got a glimpse of Mr. Rohn's journals

3695
02:21:27,040 --> 02:21:29,040
you'd have to say he is a

3696
02:21:29,040 --> 02:21:31,040
serious student.

3697
02:21:31,040 --> 02:21:33,040
Not just committed to his craft

3698
02:21:33,040 --> 02:21:35,040
but committed to life,

3699
02:21:35,040 --> 02:21:37,040
committed to skills,

3700
02:21:37,040 --> 02:21:39,040
committed to learning.

3701
02:21:39,040 --> 02:21:41,040
To see what I can do with seed and soil

3702
02:21:41,040 --> 02:21:43,040
and sunshine and rain and miracle

3703
02:21:43,040 --> 02:21:45,040
and possibilities and turn it into equities

3704
02:21:45,040 --> 02:21:47,040
of life and treasure, family relationships,

3705
02:21:47,040 --> 02:21:49,040
enterprise,

3706
02:21:49,040 --> 02:21:51,040
sales, management, gifts galore.

3707
02:21:51,040 --> 02:21:53,040
Everything you want!

3708
02:21:53,040 --> 02:21:55,040
All available, especially in America.

3709
02:21:55,040 --> 02:21:57,040
I'm asking you, keep a journal.

3710
02:21:57,040 --> 02:21:58,040
I call it one of

3711
02:21:58,040 --> 02:21:59,040
the three treasures to leave behind.

3712
02:21:59,040 --> 02:22:01,040
Let me give you that.

3713
02:22:01,040 --> 02:22:03,040
One of the three treasures to leave behind.

3714
02:22:03,040 --> 02:22:05,040
Number one is your pictures.

3715
02:22:05,040 --> 02:22:07,040
Take a lot of pictures.

3716
02:22:07,040 --> 02:22:09,040
Did you ever look back?

3717
02:22:09,040 --> 02:22:11,040
